> 20 =D1=84=D0=B5=D0=B2=D1=80. 2023 =D0=B3., =D0=B2 23:43, =
=D0=9D=D0=B8=D0=BA=D0=BE=D0=BB=D0=B0=D0=B9 =D0=98=D0=B6=D0=B8=D0=BA=D0=BE=D0=
=B2 <NIzhikov.dev@gmail.com> =D0=BD=D0=B0=D0=BF=D0=B8=D1=81=D0=B0=D0=BB(=D0=
=B0):
>=20
> Hello.
>=20
> I investigate some production failure lately and found that current =
log format for WA ZOOKEEPER-2985 [1] not aligned with ZK internal log =
format.
> Kafka print ZK session id as decimal while Zookeeper outputs using hex =
format.
>=20
> For example:
> ```
> [2023-02-01 00:42:17,590] INFO Session establishment complete on =
server some.server.name/[some_server_ip]:[server_port], sessionid =3D =
0x4002429158c0005, negotiated timeout =3D 6000 =
(org.apache.zookeeper.ClientCnxn)
> [2023-02-01 00:42:17,650] ERROR Error while creating ephemeral at =
/brokers/ids/2, node already exists and owner '144155473589174273' does =
not match current session '288270135025467397' =
(kafka.zk.KafkaZkClient$CheckedEphemeral)
> [2023-02-01 00:42:22,823] WARN Client session timed out, have not =
heard from server in 4743ms for sessionid 0x100241c44620009 =
(org.apache.zookeeper.ClientCnxn)
> ```
>=20
> Please, note that=20
> ```
> scala> java.lang.Long.toHexString(288270135025467397L)
> val res1: String =3D 4002429158c0005
>=20
> scala> java.lang.Long.toHexString(144155473589174273L)
> val res0: String =3D 20024a3b3b60001
> ```
>=20
> So =C2=AB288270135025467397=C2=BB from CheckedEphemeral log actually =
points to newly created ZK session from previous line =
=C2=AB0x4002429158c0005=C2=BB=20
> It seems more convenient to print session id in hex format.
>=20
> I prepared PR [2] to fix this.
> Please, review.
>=20
> [1] https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZOOKEEPER-2985
> [2] https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/13281
>=20


