>
>
> Our streams application shut down unexpectedly after some network issues =
that should have been easily recoverable.
> Logs:
> =C2=A0
> {code:java}
> 2022-07-29 13:39:37.854=C2=A0 INFO 25843 --- [348aefeff-admin] org.apache=
.kafka.clients.NetworkClient=C2=A0=C2=A0 : [AdminClient clientId=3DL.DII.A-=
b1355e4a-b909-4da1-a832-dd3348aefeff-admin] Disconnecting from node 3 due t=
o request timeout.
> 2022-07-29 13:39:37.854=C2=A0 INFO 25843 --- [348aefeff-admin] org.apache=
.kafka.clients.NetworkClient=C2=A0=C2=A0 : [AdminClient clientId=3DL.DII.A-=
b1355e4a-b909-4da1-a832-dd3348aefeff-admin] Cancelled in-flight METADATA re=
quest with correlation id 985 due to node 3 being disconnected (elapsed tim=
e since creation: 60023ms, elapsed time since send: 60023ms, request timeou=
t: 30000ms)
> 2022-07-29 13:39:37.867 ERROR 25843 --- [-StreamThread-1] o.a.k.s.p.i.Int=
ernalTopicManager=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 : stream-=
thread [main] Unexpected error during topic description for L.DII.A-COGROUP=
KSTREAM-AGGREGATE-STATE-STORE-0000000003-changelog.
> Error message was: org.apache.kafka.common.errors.TimeoutException: Call(=
callName=3DdescribeTopics, deadlineMs=3D1659101977830, tries=3D1, nextAllow=
edTryMs=3D1659101977955) timed out at 1659101977855 after 1 attempt(s)
> 2022-07-29 13:39:37.869=C2=A0 INFO 25843 --- [-StreamThread-1] o.a.k.s.p.=
internals.StreamThread=C2=A0=C2=A0 =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0: st=
ream-thread [L.DII.A-b1355e4a-b909-4da1-a832-dd3348aefeff-StreamThread-1] S=
tate transition from RUNNING to PENDING_SHUTDOWN
> {code}
> I think the relevant code is in [https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/31f=
f6d7f8af57e8c39061f31774a61bd1728904e/streams/src/main/java/org/apache/kafk=
a/streams/processor/internals/InternalTopicManager.java#L524|https://github=
.com/apache/kafka/blob/31ff6d7f8af57e8c39061f31774a61bd1728904e/streams/src=
/main/java/org/apache/kafka/streams/processor/internals/InternalTopicManage=
r.java#L523-L550]
> {code:java}
> topicFuture.getValue().get();{code}
> without a timeout value cannot throw a TimeoutException, so the TimeoutEx=
ception of the AdminClient will be an ExecutionException and hit the last e=
lse branch where the StreamsException is thrown.
> Possible fix:
> Use the KafkaFuture method with timeout:
> {code:java}
> public abstract T get(long timeout, TimeUnit unit) throws InterruptedExce=
ption, ExecutionException,
> TimeoutException;{code}
> instead of=C2=A0
> {code:java}
> public abstract T get() throws InterruptedException, ExecutionException;{=
code}
> =C2=A0



