> >>>> value can never be less than zero.
> >>>>
> >>>>> `.equals` default implementation on Object is by reference, so =
if the
> >>>> groupBy did not generate a new object, that may still pass. This =
means that
> >>>> even if user does not implement the `.equals` function, if the =
same object
> >>>> is returned then this feature would still be triggered, is that =
